# Query Object Conventions

- One query concern per class; public method `#call`.
- Accept context via constructor (e.g. `store:` for multi-tenant scoping).
- Return `ActiveRecord::Relation` for chainability, or `Hash` for aggregations.
- Always `includes` / `preload` / `eager_load` to prevent N+1.
- Read-only — never modify data in query objects.
- Sanitize user input: `sanitize_sql_like`, parameterized queries.
- One-liner filters stay as model scopes; extract when joins or aggregations appear.
- Test store isolation: store A cannot see store B data.
